question:
An Alternative Investment Fund (AIF Cat III / Hedge Fund) manages ₹100 Crores at the beginning of Year 1 under a '2 and 20' fee structure (2% fixed annual management fee charged on opening AUM, and a 20% incentive/performance fee charged on annual net profits above a High-Water Mark with zero hurdle rate). The fund records the following gross year-end portfolio values before fees:
Year 1: Portfolio rises to ₹130 Crores;
Year 2: Market crash causes portfolio to fall to ₹95 Crores;
Year 3: Portfolio recovers to ₹140 Crores.
What is the incentive fee payable to the fund manager at the end of Year 3?
